purpose_raw:
Funding will support senior recreational, educational, and social programming;
services such as advocacy and counseling, transportation, meals, and health
promotion; and general operating expenses for such programming and services.

To support core program including Buddy 2 Buddy Peer Caregiver Support program;
to provide health and wellness activities; and to sustain the "Still Standing: Aging
Gracefully and Positively" Initiative.

To fund cultural enrichment programs, including an oral history project;
presentations, and walking tours on the history, culture, and ecology of Coney Island;
and visits to the History Project by school and community groups.

To provide funding support for education reform, equity, green/open spaces;
retrofitting for energy efficiency; and mapping arts resources. Funds will support
staffing, space rental, training materials, and facilitation of community events.

Funding to support Senior Service Program including: translation services;
educational classes of: ESL, naturalization, crime prevention, computer, Tai Chi;
activities: recreation / social gathering, cultural holiday celebration; daily hot lunches.

Funding to provide assistance to tenants and homeowners; services include eviction
prevention, information re: the rights & responsibilities of tenants and owners;
assistance with housing subsidies.

Funding to support expenses related to the Annual Essay, Poetry & Art Contest;
Family Day Awards Celebration including books, art supplies, MLK t-shirts, promotion,
printing, postage, food, storage, and photography.
